# Drafted by Gemini (R20), edited. R20: the village after Golub: the new postmaster, the constable, the Druskenvalds' repairs.

~ geneva_postmaster
Narrator: Geneva Fairchild stands behind the scrubbed oak counter, a little thinner in the face, her lilac eyes shadowed with fatigue but clear at last.
geneva_fairchild [sad]: I remember shouting at you in the street, though I cannot for the life of me say why. The keys are mine now, and I mean to run this office strictly by the book.
* Tell her the madness was none of her doing. -> geneva_forgive
* Ask what she remembers of Theodora Mayville. -> geneva_remember
* Wish her well with the new post. -> END
~ geneva_forgive
approve tobin_hayward +2 lucan_houndstooth +1 cordelia_skein -1: You told Geneva the madness was none of her doing
set rk_geneva_back
geneva_fairchild [smile]: Thank you for saying so. I swear I will read every letter once, and never twice.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Proper procedure, that. Once for the stamp, and straight into the sack.
-> END
~ geneva_remember
geneva_fairchild [afraid]: Miss Theodora told me once that lilac eyes were a mark of luck, not a curse. Even knowing what she was, that remains the nicest thing anyone ever said to me.
-> geneva_postmaster

~ wynn
Narrator: A broad-shouldered young inn hand stands behind the counter, sorting bundles of post with enormous, slow care as if the paper might bite.
wynn_carter [smile]: Somebody had to take the keys after the trouble, and nobody else wanted the work. I have read the postal rules twice already, and I mean to read them again before supper.
* Ask how he came to take the job. -> wynn_how
* Wish him luck with the letters. -> END
~ wynn_how
wynn_carter [weary]: Mistress Alda Farnum put my name forward because I know my letters and I know how to keep quiet. I did not realize at the time she meant that as a warning.
-> wynn

~ doris_after
set rk_doris_after
Narrator: Constable Doris Squire stands amid the splintered wood and cold ash of the Round, her cap set straight, looking from the wreckage down to her own broad hands.
doris_squire [weary]: I remember all of it, and I would sooner I did not. I am sorry for my part in it, and I do not say that twice.
if flag.jail_key_left
doris_squire [sad]: Somebody read a few lines of my verse while I was out of my head, and was kind about it. I have not decided how I feel about that yet.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The cadence was remarkably sound, Constable, if you will forgive the intrusion.
endif
-> END

~ phillip_repairs
Narrator: Phillip Druskenvald stands in a dapper coat free of soot, pressing heavy leather purses into the hands of a line of villagers who cannot quite meet his eye.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Take heart, good friends, for the Druskenvalds shall rebuild all that this madness broke, down to the very last shutter. It is the least a proper landowner can do.
set rk_repairs_paid
-> END

~ adela_worry
Narrator: Adela Druskenvald stands in the chill lane with her hands tucked deep into her sleeves, watching a steep roof where a few grey pigeons have settled.
adela_druskenvald [afraid]: Maybe the bird trouble is over, darling, but I had the foulest dream last night about a great laughing sun. I can tell you right now, I did not like the look of it at all.
-> END
